          "call_cd15a313b6a84dba90a587dbec3c001a"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Read the introducing models chapter at 543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff and the component-interface entry at 830b6a018070a327d6d261628dff496f1303cf93. They establish the Gemma2 construction pattern and the named-component/compiler-hook interface reused here. The former records Gemma2's sliding_window_size mismatch; the latter records an incomplete Qwen3 MoE component migration.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_21203636ef8342dc99d6e7ca573e722b",
          "call_c6a27687de5c42ffb3ef695a6ea035d2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "The new Gemma3 path reads text_config->sliding_window, rather than copying Gemma2's sliding_window_size lookup. Gemma2 itself is unchanged. The Qwen3 MoE interface mismatch also persists, as recorded separately in findings.",
        "basis": "source",
