    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Gemma3 text assembly and component preservation",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Registration uses Gemma3Config.arch_string = Gemma3ForConditionalGeneration. Config.from_directory selects it from the single architectures entry; Model.from_config defaults to the text component. The new mapping supplies both Gemma3Model and Gemma3VisionModel, but only the text class assembles executable modules. This does not register Gemma3ForCausalLM.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3208bceabb864ba78375da651462bb78",
              "call_0ce81ed200e6422cb7f20de51383aebc",
              "call_724414d2227f48a49aa519be35d8aece",
              "call_051b4483066341e4ab7e3cfdaa3c9c2b",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Gemma3Config reads decoder dimensions, layer count, normalization and attention options under text_config. Layer count and the text_config dictionary are required. The base Config already searches both top-level and nested vocab_size; Gemma3 supplies 262208 only when neither yields a value. read_dict accepts integer-valued floating-point settings and treats null like an absent value, so explicit null softcaps select the adapter's zero defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_724414d2227f48a49aa519be35d8aece",
              "call_604a94796d3c415a81232f943cb1539e",
              "call_782bcde0e9374bfea6890729894d0a9c",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "read_rope_settings_default gains optional theta, partial-rotation and source-dictionary arguments without changing its RopeSettings return form. None selects self.config_dict; an explicitly empty dictionary remains empty. Whole-tree search found ten existing callers: Cohere, Cohere2, DeciLM, Gemma2, GLM4, Llama, Mixtral, Phi3, Qwen3 and Qwen3 MoE. Each still supplies only its original RopeStyle and retains the previous defaults. No other read_cfg definition was found, so the replacement with read_dict bypasses no inspected subclass override.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_de57fe284431446dba1b56f46eb2e3c5",
              "call_3251a73b8011477995917b9ceb50028d",
              "call_788828d6edef41e7b64dd374c86917f3",
              "call_45b7e406dc58464faea408ee8c4d86cc",
              "call_45bcb02350cd4f4894ab1e54f19148e3"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Global RoPE reads text_config with a default base of 1000000. Local RoPE reads an empty dictionary with base 10000, full rotation and no scaling. Both use NEOX style. These bases govern inverse frequencies, not context-length thresholds. For the reference configurations' linear factor 8, RoPE._rope_params_linear divides global inverse frequencies by eight; the local settings avoid that division.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_de57fe284431446dba1b56f46eb2e3c5",
              "call_3182aa72184b4da28cc653b61581817d",
              "call_daa996e56c424d1c87d7718372f61f84",
              "call_74e9e98f59164e22999625e3a431aeac",
              "call_7b68986b1b924a6b83ec3a0ed103827f",
              "call_8ffad3fae74340eaa3aef20f858b22a5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "bool((idx + 1) % sliding_window_pattern) selects local attention. With the default pattern 6, five local blocks precede each unrestricted block. Local blocks receive sliding_window and local RoPE; global blocks receive -1 and global RoPE. The adapter's fallback window is 4096, whereas every inspected reference configuration explicitly supplies 1024. Attention forwards these values to FlashAttention's window_size; its SDPA alternative asserts against nonnegative windows and therefore is not interchangeable for the ordinary Gemma3 pattern.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_eb011aacc52d47c38c93c5e7468d2797",
              "call_7a7cfd8f656c4b76b0224638cd20cd9e",
              "call_61662475e4a0472088332d7e1e407e4a",
              "call_35320a492e494a0ba8ae31e739a9e689",
              "call_7d72a5e5e1f240b0b8e681aace83b99e"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The text sequence is language_model.model.embed_tokens, decoder blocks under language_model.model.layers.i, language_model.model.norm and language_model.lm_head. Embedding normalization multiplies activations by sqrt(hidden_size). Each block places input normalization before attention, post-attention normalization before its residual addition, pre-feedforward normalization before the GELU gated MLP, and post-feedforward normalization before its residual addition. All these RMSNorms use weight + 1; branch post-norms request float output.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_ce498dd27c384f26ab3bd5c21a61585e",
              "call_e0a98ecbca444e6b9f076f1532c48678",
              "call_e8fcfccf934a4d62b790d7b7b45c4b09",
              "call_a0a612bfdeae4a5faffb2a3c870ddc11"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Attention applies the supplied Q/K RMSNorms after reshaping projections into heads and before RoPE; their vectors therefore have head_dim elements, not hidden_size elements. FlashAttention receives query_pre_attn_scalar**(-0.5) as softmax_scale. The head always offers the embedding as an alternate tensor key, independently of the stored tie_word_embeddings flag. Linear first tries EXL3 storage, then ordinary weights; ordinary checkpoint matrices are transposed when loaded.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_7a7cfd8f656c4b76b0224638cd20cd9e",
              "call_c55a4bf8435943608518de30111155d1"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All eleven listed Gemma3 configurations were read. google/gemma-3-4b-it and google/gemma-3-4b-pt map to hidden/intermediate widths 2560/10240 and 34 layers; their omitted head settings use the adapter's defaults D=256, Q=8 and K=4. google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-4b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized explicitly supply those same head dimensions. Each supplies window 1024 and global linear scaling factor 8. The QAT files explicitly confirm vocabulary 262208, theta 1000000, local base 10000 and pattern 6; the compact IT/PT files rely on adapter defaults for those omitted values.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_61662475e4a0472088332d7e1e407e4a",
              "call_535d509ad1cc4bd1b5ee856c44c7b0cf",
              "call_e78556794f0245edb3f45a856bbc6103",
              "call_08f066b816fd478e844a6ace57ff03d3",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-12b-it and google/gemma-3-12b-pt supply widths 3840/15360, 48 layers, Q=16 and K=8, using default D=256 and attention scalar 256. google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-int4-unquantized and google/gemma-3-12b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized explicitly confirm those settings. Each maps window 1024 and global linear factor 8. As for 4B, the QAT configurations explicitly provide the vocabulary, RoPE bases and pattern corresponding to the adapter defaults; their null softcaps map to zero.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_35320a492e494a0ba8ae31e739a9e689",
              "call_0fd081562dd546a18c33ad2b8052ff5c",
              "call_cb11a59da918414fab93fbd8930d54c2",
              "call_0b723a0a17514d5597ea1be38fbd33eb",
              "call_604a94796d3c415a81232f943cb1539e",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "google/gemma-3-27b-it, google/gemma-3-27b-pt and google/gemma-3-27b-it-qat-q4_0-unquantized each supply widths 5376/21504, 62 layers, D=128, Q=32, K=16 and attention scalar 168. Thus the adapter must honor explicit head_dim rather than derive it from hidden_size/Q. Each supplies window 1024 and linear factor 8. The QAT configuration explicitly confirms the same vocabulary, RoPE bases and pattern defaults and uses null softcaps. These configuration artifacts are hash-verified mirror files, not runtime compatibility tests.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7d72a5e5e1f240b0b8e681aace83b99e",
              "call_9758ca3ac23140fda667ee37fef44e18",
              "call_e661d91bb24a41a7964a6c2133a761fb",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The 4B IT headers contain all 34 layers' requested q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj, gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj, four block norms and Q/K norms, plus embedding and final norm. Shapes are Q [2048,2560], K/V [1024,2560], O [2560,2048], gate/up [10240,2560], down [2560,10240], block norms [2560] and Q/K norms [256]. Embedding is [262208,2560]. The text inventory has no separate language_model.lm_head.weight, optional linear biases or EXL3 groups, so the inspected loader selects ordinary weights and the embedding fallback for the head.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_e7dbeb09f18745bd8cf0edfa763f2013",
              "call_19f81bcbdfd44a31b3fa007a7e402675",
              "call_f8d82d8ee12343d491499bc9df2ee353",
              "call_c55a4bf8435943608518de30111155d1",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "First-layer header samples also match the configured projection dimensions for 12B and 27B. For 12B, Q/K/O are [4096,3840], [2048,3840], [3840,4096], with gate/up [15360,3840], down [3840,15360] and Q/K norms [256]. For 27B they are [4096,5376], [2048,5376], [5376,4096], [21504,5376], [5376,21504] and [128]. Their sampled embeddings are [262208,3840] and [262208,5376]. All sampled tensors are BF16.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_2aa89261e1da42d4abdeef7aa915d0ae",
              "call_4b8e1f43748f4c73a0be3eb458446dcc",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A scalar transcription of the layer-selection formula yields 29 local/5 global blocks for 4B, 40/8 for 12B and 52/10 for 27B. Global zero-based indices start at 5 and advance by six. Dimension arithmetic matches the sampled projection shapes; attention scales evaluate to 0.0625 for 4B/12B and approximately 0.077151675 for 27B. Separately, executing the repository read_dict utility confirmed that a null floating-point key returns the supplied zero default.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_c9561144c34c4d56be689f103ba60506"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Gemma3Model.prepare_inputs follows every inspected existing architecture caller: retain input_ids in params and call prepare_for_attn with the same arguments. That helper retains its existing backend/cache checks. The new Q/K normalization similarly uses Attention's existing paired-norm mechanism; both norms are supplied, satisfying its assertion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5ff48970d4eb4b69a5be957b11b4cb9f",
              "call_0fc43b586a104154814ab354c9523434",
              "call_7a7cfd8f656c4b76b0224638cd20cd9e",
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The vision class is a preservation hook, not a vision forward implementation: load and unload raise NotImplementedError. Its static hook unions list_tensors results for vision_tower and multi_modal_projector. The prior list_tensors caller in quantization metadata passes a module prefix with the same exact-or-dot-descendant semantics; the new calls retain its assertion against active new_tensors. compile_model invokes hooks on all configured classes without instantiating vision, then copies returned tensors from config.stc with BF16 allowed. The 4B header includes mm_input_projection_weight [1152,2560], mm_soft_emb_norm.weight [1152] and vision-tower tensors that the text forward path never consumes.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_cd97aed8cc224d729b0a911f68e7908f",
              "call_eb80998def40401fad2751696f22d0b7",
              "call_0797ccaa5e13451ba6893d3d3fcef7a0",
              "call_66e532f59b66442581a225e8f9c573c8",
              "call_cd15a313b6a84dba90a587dbec3c001a",
              "call_19f81bcbdfd44a31b3fa007a7e402675"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Preserving those additional tensors appears intended to avoid making text-only conversion discard the future multimodal components. This interpretation follows the component hook and copied namespaces; it does not establish implemented multimodal inference or an explicit author rationale.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_27d2297897b64655a9b89f49e5eece61",
              "call_cd15a313b6a84dba90a587dbec3c001a"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
